            <ArticleTitle>Efavirenz to nevirapine switch in HIV-1-infected patients with dyslipidemia: a randomized, controlled study.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many antiretroviral therapies, including efavirenz, are associated with increased serum concentrations of low-density lipoprotein cholesterol. In a small 52-week randomized study, we found that switching from efavirenz to nevirapine was associated with significantly decreased low-density lipoprotein cholesterol levels, compared with continuation of efavirenz therapy (P&lt;.04). A switch to nevirapine was associated with no severe adverse events.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
